Committed. The fourth door on the trust boundary is closed.

What shipped (src/cli.rs, CLAUDE.md, tests/module_size.rs):

• **gate_project_hooks(hooks, project_local, trusted)** — pure, refuses only when the loaded config is project-local *and* `--trust-project` wasn't passed. Every other input is a byte-identical pass-through.
• `project_hook_refusal_message` — names each refused hook as pre.bash = <command> (the shape it has in the file, so a user can grep for it), command verbatim, capped at 400 bytes on a char boundary with the cut marked in band, both escape hatches, and "Nothing was executed." said outright. Glyph-free under is_plain_output(), silent under is_quiet().
• One call site wrapping the old parse_hooks_from_config line.

The direction argument in the issue was wrong and I said so in the code. #820's body (which I wrote during assessment) claimed a blocking hooks.pre.* *restricts yoyo, so the gate should spare it. It doesn't survive the mechanism: a pre-hook produces its blocking effect by running arbitrary shell first*. The Day-166 asymmetry sorts **declarative** values yoyo interprets (`permissions.deny`, `dir_restrictions` — kept verbatim, a repo may always confine me further); a hook's entire content is executable code. Both phases refused.

Second door checked, needed nothing. handle_hooks is reached only from dispatch.rs:829 → ctx.agent_config.shell_hooks → main.rs:943 → config.shell_hooks, the gated vec. Traced rather than assumed; commands_config.rs untouched.

Verified live, not just by unit test — three real configs through the built binary: project-local untrusted → refused with both commands printed; --trust-project → no refusal; the same hooks moved to ~/.yoyo.toml → untouched.

Tests: four-combination table on the gate (including the pass-through side — a discriminator tested only where it blocks is vacuous green), emission-point assertions on the message string a caller receives, plain-output glyph check, and a truncation test with multi-byte input plus its under-budget near-miss. build, test (5074 + integration), clippy -D warnings, fmt --check all green.

One honest cost: src/cli.rs went 4325 → 4570 lines, so I paid the register entry my own module-size gate asked for rather than absorbing it.
